# NestJS — Project Conventions

This is the **NestJS 10** backend in the Tripteki parallel-codebase family. It shares one REST contract and the same event names with FastAPI. Nuxt and Next can use either backend. The product brand is **Codebase**.

## Family conventions

| Topic | Rule |
|-------|------|
| Roles | Exactly `superadmin`, `admin`, `user` through `UserRoleEnum` |
| Brand | `APP_NAME` Codebase. Primary `#2563eb`, secondary `#84cc16`, tertiary `#1e3a8a` |
| Locales | `en`, `id`, `ms` under `src/app/langs/` |
| GraphQL | Sources stay in the tree. `AppGraphqlProvider` is not booted |
| Mongo | Off when `DATABASE_MONGO_URI` is empty |
| Rate limit | Production only (`app.env !== production` skips the throttler) |
| Format | Indent 4, double quotes, trailing commas, space before `(` |
| Docs | Keep JSDoc |
| Principles | SOLID, dependency injection, tight cohesion and loose coupling |
| Patterns | Repository, validator/transformer DTO, middleware, observer (events and listeners) |

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Framework | NestJS 10 + TypeScript (strict, SWC builder) |
| Runtime | **Bun** (`bun run`); README may still reference npm |
| ORM | Prisma — PostgreSQL migrations. MongoDB only when `DATABASE_MONGO_URI` is set |
| Cache/Queue | Redis — cache, Bull job queues |
| REST | Swagger at `/api/docs` |
| GraphQL | Apollo sources exist. `/graphql` is not mounted |
| WebSockets | Socket.IO — room-based emits to `user:{id}` |
| Auth | JWT — access + refresh tokens |
| Mail | Handlebars templates via Nest mailer |
| i18n | nestjs-i18n — `en`, `id`, `ms` |
| Scheduler | `@nestjs/schedule` |

## Directory layout

```
src/
  app/                          # Infrastructure layer
    configs/                    # registerAs config modules
    providers/                  # Boot providers (AppHttpProvider, etc.)
    drivers/                    # External service drivers
    databases/                  # Prisma clients
    helpers/                    # Shared utilities
    langs/                      # i18n files
  v1/
    api/{domain}/               # REST domain modules
      controllers/
      services/
      repositories/
      dtos/                     # validator, transformer, enum
      events/
      listeners/
      processors/               # Bull queue processors
      middlewares/
      modules/
      databases/
      views/                    # Email templates
    graphql/{domain}/           # Parallel GraphQL stack
      resolvers/
      services/
      dtos/
      middlewares/
      modules/
test/                           # E2E tests only (*.e2e-spec.ts)
  test.case.ts                  # setupTestApp, setupAuthTestApp
storage/logs/
public/
```

## Naming conventions

| Artifact | Convention | Example |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| File | dot-separated lowercase | `user.auth.service.ts` |
| Class | PascalCase | `UserAuthService` |
| Event | PascalCase + Event suffix | `UserAuthLoggedInEvent` |
| Validator DTO | `*.validator.dto.ts` | `user.validator.dto.ts` |
| Transformer DTO | `*.transformer.dto.ts` | `user.transformer.dto.ts` |
| Enum | `*.enum.ts` | `user-role.enum.ts` |
| Import path | Absolute from `src/` | `import { X } from 'src/app/...'` |

No `@` path alias in tsconfig — always use `src/...` imports.

## Shared API contract (all backends)

### Endpoints
- REST base: `/api/v1` (global prefix `api` plus controller paths that already include `v1`)
- Swagger docs: `/api/docs`
- GraphQL is not mounted
- Health/status: `/api/status`

### Auth
- `POST /api/v1/auth/login` returns HTTP 201 `{ accessToken, refreshToken, accessTokenTtl, refreshTokenTtl }`
- Login body is `{ identifierKey, identifierValue, password, remember }`; `identifierKey` is `email` or `name` (optional, inferred from `@`)
- `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh`, `POST /api/v1/auth/register`, `POST /api/v1/auth/logout`
- Profile is `GET` and `PUT /api/v1/users/me`
- Signed pages on the frontend are `/auth/reset-password/{email}` and `/auth/verify-email/{email}`

### Error responses
```json
// Validation (HTTP 422), same detail shape as FastAPI
{ "detail": [{ "type": "string_too_short", "loc": ["body", "password"], "msg": "String should have at least 8 characters", "input": "123", "ctx": { "min_length": 8 } }] }

// Other HTTP exceptions (AppHttpExceptionFilter), same as FastAPI and Laravel
{ "detail": "Invalid credentials" }
```

### Pagination
```json
{ "total": 0, "totalPage": 1, "perPage": 10, "currentPage": 1, "nextPage": null, "previousPage": null, "firstPage": 1, "lastPage": 1, "data": [] }
```

### Rate limiting
- Throttle applies in **production only** (`app.env === production`)
- Do not throttle in development or tests

## Environment variables

```
APP_NAME, APP_SECRET, APP_PORT, APP_ENV, APP_LOCALE, APP_TIMEZONE
FRONTEND_URL
NODE_ENV
MEMORY_REDIS_HOST, MEMORY_REDIS_PORT, MEMORY_REDIS_PASSWORD
DATABASE_POSTGRE_URI, DATABASE_MONGO_URI
MAIL_URI
SWAGGER_TITLE, SWAGGER_DESCRIPTION, SWAGGER_VERSION
```

Config loaded via `@nestjs/config` `registerAs()` in `src/app/configs/`.

## Setup commands

```bash
bun install
bun run prisma              # Generate Prisma clients
bun run postgre:migrate     # PostgreSQL migrations
bun run mongo:migrate       # MongoDB schema push, only when DATABASE_MONGO_URI is set
bun run dev                 # Start dev server
bun run build               # Production build
```

## Testing

```bash
bun test                    # Jest e2e watch mode
bun run test:e2e            # Jest e2e with coverage
```

- **E2E only** — no unit test suite; do not add unit tests unless requested
- **Requires Redis** running at `127.0.0.1:6379` for e2e tests
- Default test user: `superuser@mail.com` / `12345678`
- Helpers: `setupTestApp()`, `setupAuthTestApp()` in `test/test.case.ts`

## Lint

```bash
bun run lint    # Prettier + ESLint (@tripteki/eslint-config, @tripteki/prettier-config)
```
